    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0190" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v04/pg162"/>

                <head>52. Message From the Secretary of State to the
                        President<anchor n="1" xml:id="d52-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1956-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                        1956</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: The work of the Council is
                    now over except for preparing the communiqué<anchor n="2" xml:id="d52-f2"/>
                    which as you know is always troublesome and will be so this afternoon.</p>
                <p>I believe the results have been all that could reasonably have been expected. The
                    recommendations of the three Ministers for developing NATO have been unanimously adopted including a proposal for
                    settlement of disputes between members.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d52-f3"/></p>
                <p>The Directive to the military which this year was particularly serious and
                    controversial has been adopted.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d52-f4"/>
                    Wilson’s statement on the military annual
                    review made today<anchor n="5" xml:id="d52-f5"/> was, I think, a good statement,
                    at least as could have been made given the internal differences of opinion.…</p>
                <p>We have in informal talks done much to regain the sense of unity which was
                    dissipated by the attack on Egypt although obviously some scars and resentments
                    still remain.</p>
                <pb facs="0191" n="163" xml:id="pg163"/>
                <p>Ismay’s resignation was accepted in which
                    connection I expressed on your behalf your personal regard for him and his
                    services. Spaak was elected to succeed
                        him.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d52-f6"/></p>
                <p>As always at these conferences the informal contacts between the Ministers have
                    provided the most profitable aspect of the meeting.</p>
                <p>I shall report more fully when I see you soon.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d52-f7"/></p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Foster</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d52-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d52-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 110.11–DU/12–1456. Secret; Priority.
                    Transmitted to Washington in Dulte 19,
                    December 14, at 4 p.m. The copy of the telegram in the Eisenhower Library,
                        Whitman File, Dulles–Herter Series,
                    bears the President’s initials.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f2" n="2" xml:id="d52-f2-content">
                <p>For text of the final communiqué, dated December 14, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, December 24 and 31, 1956, p. 981.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f3" n="3" xml:id="d52-f3-content">
                <p>For text of the Report of the Committee of Three on Non-Military Co-operation in
                        NATO and the Resolution on the Peaceful
                    Settlement of Disputes and Differences Between Members of the North Atlantic
                    Treaty Organization, both dated December 14, see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>, January 7, 1957, pp. 17–28.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f4" n="4" xml:id="d52-f4-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d49-f3">footnote 3, Document 49</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f5" n="5" xml:id="d52-f5-content">
                <p>See Polto 1424, <ref target="#d51"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f6" n="6" xml:id="d52-f6-content">
                <p>Ismay announced his decision to retire on
                    December 14, 1956. Spaak did not assume
                    responsibilities as Secretary General of NATO
                    until May 16, 1957.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f7" n="7" xml:id="d52-f7-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d54">Document 54</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
